<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Celtillus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 1st century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Celtillus was a leading noble of the Arverni in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> in the early 1st century BCE and the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>, he held the chief power in all Gaul but was put to death by his own people for seeking to make himself king.</p></div>
